\id PSA Transparent Bible (working title) - pilot draft
\h Psalms
\toc1 The Book of Psalms
\toc2 Psalms
\toc3 Ps
\mt1 Psalms
\c 23
\d A Psalm of David.
\q1
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* is my shepherd;
\q2 I shall not lack.\f + \fr 23:1 \ft Note: KJV \fqa I shall not want\ft , where “want” means “lack”.\f*
\q1
\v 2 He makes me lie down in green pastures;
\q2 he leads me beside still waters.\f + \fr 23:2 \ft Lit.: \fqa waters of rest\f*
\q1
\v 3 He restores my soul;
\q2 he leads me in paths of righteousness
\q2 for his name’s sake.\f + \fr 23:3 \ft Heb.: \fqa nephesh\ft , “soul”, also “life”, “self”. Or: \fqa he brings me back\ft .\f*\f + \fr 23:3 \ft Or: \fqa right paths\ft .\f*
\q1
\v 4 Even though I walk through the valley of deep darkness,
\q2 I will fear no evil,
\q1 for you are with me;
\q2 your rod and your staff, they comfort me.\f + \fr 23:4 \ft Heb.: \fqa tsalmavet\ft , traditionally read as “shadow of death” (KJV); the word means thick darkness. Or: \fqa a valley of deep darkness\ft , not one valley in particular.\f*
\q1
\v 5 You prepare a table before me
\q2 in the presence of my enemies;
\q1 you have anointed my head with oil;
\q2 my cup overflows.\f + \fr 23:5 \ft Lit.: \fqa you have made my head rich with oil\ft ; not the verb used for anointing kings and priests.\f*\f + \fr 23:5 \ft Lit.: \fqa my cup is overflowing fullness\f*
\q1
\v 6 Surely goodness and steadfast love shall follow me\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Or: \fqa pursue me\ft . The Hebrew verb is the ordinary word for chasing.\f*
\q2 all the days of my life,
\q1 and I will dwell in the house of the \nd LORD\nd*
\q2 for length of days.\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Heb.: \fqa hesed\ft , love that keeps covenant; KJV \fqa mercy\ft , elsewhere \fqa lovingkindness\ft .\f*\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Heb.: as pointed, \fqa I will return to the house\ft ; the Greek (LXX), the KJV and most translations read the verb as “dwell”.\f*\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Heb.: \fqa ’orekh yamim\ft , “length of days”, that is, a long life; KJV \fqa for ever\ft .\f*
